    },
    {
      "id": "person:speaker-02",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Dr. Elena Fischer"
      },
      "type": "Person"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:9ac58e514db2c89e",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 372,
        "char_start": 248,
        "episode_id": "5ef53e66-e083-5fcb-b555-a3814ebb6b39",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "Thanks, Alex Morgan. Excited for this one \u2014 sustainability and systems thinking is something I've been thinking about a lot.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 12000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 6000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p07_e01.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "person:speaker-01",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Alex Morgan"
      },
      "type": "Person"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:e6cee099d2202230",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 504,
        "char_start": 386,
        "episode_id": "5ef53e66-e083-5fcb-b555-a3814ebb6b39",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "Today's episode is sponsored by Notion. Notion replaces the dozen tools your team is half-using. Try notion.com today.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 18000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 12000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p07_e01.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:2568bfce550feac8",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 584,
        "char_start": 504,
        "episode_id": "5ef53e66-e083-5fcb-b555-a3814ebb6b39",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "That's a useful framing. Where do systems thinking and sustainability intersect?",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 24000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 18000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p07_e01.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:2d58317ca7a95e57",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 846,
        "char_start": 604,
        "episode_id": "5ef53e66-e083-5fcb-b555-a3814ebb6b39",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "Let me give you the version I actually believe. Sustainability is a systems-thinking problem before it's an environmental problem. We've seen this play out at teams using Carbon Trust. And the second-order effect is the part most people miss.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 30000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 24000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p07_e01.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:8a74a9c3241c3596",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 942,
        "char_start": 860,
        "episode_id": "5ef53e66-e083-5fcb-b555-a3814ebb6b39",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "That's a useful framing. What's the version of the question that actually matters?",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 36000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 30000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p07_e01.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:9057f2a2ac9f099b",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 1128,
        "char_start": 962,
        "episode_id": "5ef53e66-e083-5fcb-b555-a3814ebb6b39",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "Here's how I think about it. The most expensive thing about climate is the optionality you lose by delaying. And the second-order effect is the part most people miss.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 42000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 36000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p07_e01.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    }
  ],
